        "text": "brainstorming:\n\u2022 A friend was fooling with a midi/mixer control surface as a layered interface to a bank of apps/subdirectories. A grid of buttons, push into one then get a sub-grid of buttons within it, or, open the app.\n\u2022 IMO, software is just soft hardware. What ideas come to mind for simulating a Z controller before committing to hardware? It seems that an obvious choice might be to put a 2nd scroll bar next to the Y scroll bar. The 2nd scroll bar might be \"Z\"oom in/out and it might be shaped in a more triangular manner than just a rectangular movable thumb on a rectangular bar. In an orthogonal vein: <@UC2A2ARPT> posted some interesting looking circular knob ideas.\n\u2022 2 sliders, one to control scrollable thing, one to control resolution of 1st slider.\n\u2022 veering even further away from the original thread, there are ZUIs like <https://eaglemode.sourceforge.net|EagleMode>.",
